WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.043
- Alright.

00:00:01.043 --> 00:00:02.520
I like to find the most
heartwarming stories

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.080
from the internet and share them here.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:04.984
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:04.984 --> 00:00:07.139
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:08.220
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:09.240
If you've ever lived

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.790
in an apartment with thin walls, I have.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:15.390
And you know that your business
is everyone else's as well.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.223
Very thin walls.

00:00:16.223 --> 00:00:17.790
We can hear you arguing.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:20.460
So what do you do if
your newborn cries a lot?

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.600
Well, you should take a page

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.210
from this New York couple
who posted a peace offering

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.500
on their front door.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.970
It reads, we have a newborn.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.800
He is loud, we are sorry.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.340
He's cute as (beep), but very noisy.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.173
Bear with us.

00:00:33.173 --> 00:00:34.170
Thanks to your patience.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:35.927
Take a nip or two at your leisure.

00:00:35.927 --> 00:00:38.968
And below the sign is a bucket of alcohol.

00:00:38.968 --> 00:00:39.840
(audience laughing)

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.760
These are my kind of people.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.160
Let's get these very
considerate parents in here.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.540
Meet Kristen and Todd watching

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.044
on NBC4 in New York everybody.

00:00:47.044 --> 00:00:47.877
(audience clapping)

00:00:47.877 --> 00:00:49.620
Oh my god, the little one.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.730
Well, Kristen and Todd first,
congrats on the new baby. Oh.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:54.563
So where did you--

00:00:54.563 --> 00:00:55.590
- Thank you.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:56.940
- Where did y'all get this idea

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.740
to give your neighbors some
alcohol so they'll be happy?

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:03.600
- He's really, really loud

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.240
and alcohol can solve many problems

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.040
when things get stressful.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.710
So figured it'd be a nice peace offering.

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:13.470
- Yeah. Todd was out doing
his laundry in the elevator

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.720
and could hear how loud Quint was.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.120
- Yeah, I could hear him
screaming from our elevator

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.270
while I was doing laundry and I ran inside

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.500
and was like I'm going to make a sign

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.580
and we're going to a liquor store.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:26.940
And we have like a little bucket that

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.490
like a little bathrobe for him came in

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:30.690
that I just filled with nips

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.060
and attached it to our front door.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:34.560
And the rest is history.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.120
I think our neighbors enjoyed it.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.820
Social media seemed to
enjoy it, so we're happy.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:39.849
- [Kelly] Cause it's thoughtful.

00:01:39.849 --> 00:01:42.113
- And he seems to be happy too.

00:01:42.113 --> 00:01:43.620
- I wish I was that
kind of happy right now.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:46.050
That's a slumber I haven't
experienced in a minute.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:50.310
So Todd, is it possible
Quint takes after you

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.720
because like aren't you a musician?

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:52.770
Are you kinda loud?

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:53.603
- Yeah, I'm loud.

00:01:53.603 --> 00:01:57.150
I'm a special education
music teacher in Brooklyn.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.650
I like to hear myself talk.

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:01.560
I've been playing in punk rock
bands for like two decades.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.930
I currently play in a band
called United Blood NYC.

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:05.070
You can find us on Instagram.

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:06.360
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:10.740
- And if you like what you
see, follow Milk Stain NYC.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:11.866
That's our family.

00:02:11.866 --> 00:02:12.797
- I love that.

00:02:12.797 --> 00:02:14.327
- [Kristen] Thanks Kelly.

00:02:14.327 --> 00:02:15.160
(audience clapping)

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:17.130
- Well, congratulations on your family

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:18.300
and also congratulations

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.093
on being respectable kind
neighbors and thoughtful.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.910
Thank you so much, Kristen.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:24.960
Thank you Todd.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.280
Thank you Quint.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.560
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:29.393
And that's not all y'all.

00:02:29.393 --> 00:02:31.800
Our season long partner,
Pilot pen makers of G2,

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.390
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:35.662
want to honor considerate
people like yourselves.

00:02:35.662 --> 00:02:37.830
So they're gonna be helping
you by writing you a check

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.064
for a thousand dollars so you
can replenish that alcohol.

00:02:40.064 --> 00:02:42.624
(audience cheering)

00:02:42.624 --> 00:02:44.184
- Thank you.

00:02:44.184 --> 00:02:45.570
- Thank you guys so much.

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:47.190
And thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:49.140
Keanu Reeves, Ian McShane,

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:51.450
Lance Reddick, Shamier Anderson,

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:56.220
Hiroyuki Sanada, and also Chad
Stahelski and Emily Kaufman.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.180
Y'all have a great day

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.520
and if it's not we'll try and change it.

